; coverage test for automatic chain transitivity (see chain-transitivity-is-automatic.kurt)
; applied to equality.kurt's `chain =` and prop.kurt's `chain iff implies` -- confirms the
; feature isn't specific to numeric order relations. The `implies`+`implies` case is a genuine
; (if narrow) win against kurt's usual single-hop-derivation limitation: plain implication
; chaining now needs no manual intermediate step either.
load equality
var a, b, c
use a = b
use b = c
a = c

load prop
bool A, B, C
use A implies B
use B implies C
A implies C
;;; Proof checked.
